a secret can arrive in a log by accident — an error quoting a request,
a tool argument echoed back. Redaction is the last line, not the first.

  before: POST /v1/messages failed: header x-api-key=sk-ant-api03-NOTAREALKEY-000000000000000000000000 rejected
  after:  POST /v1/messages failed: header x-api-key=<anthropic redacted> rejected

-- a short secret is NOT redacted: it would match everywhere and turn
   ordinary text into a wall of markers.
  the answer is 42, on line 42

-- and the summary shows names and LENGTHS, never a prefix: the first
   four characters of an API key identify the provider and the account.
secrets: ready
  stored: 2
    anthropic (49 chars)
    pin (2 chars)
